 ## Overview
-A hierarchical raycasting algorithm that traverses a sparse shadow volume texture to find the first intersection with a shadow-casting volume [S1, unofficial]. It dynamically adjusts its traversal step size and level of detail (LOD) based on occupancy bits, allowing it to skip empty space efficiently compared to fixed-step hierarchical variants [S1, unofficial]. It differs from siblings such as [Voxel-Cell Duality Mapping](2240-voxel-cell-duality-mapping.md), [Spherical Volume Ray Walking](3865-spherical-volume-ray-walking.md), [Plane Marching](3959-plane-marching.md), [RLE4 Ray Tracing](5228-rle4-ray-tracing.md), [Regular Grid Traversal](5939-regular-grid-traversal.md), [Voxel Raytracer](6403-voxel-raytracer.md), and [DirectVoxGO Volume Rendering](6412-directvoxgo-volume-rendering.md) by using a multi-level occupancy-bit search that refines or coarsens traversal granularity on the fly.
